    rdfs:label "ifr:ReleaseRecord"@en ;
    mz:basis mz:Specializes ;
    mz:definedBy "0026-works-versioning FR-008" ;
    mz:justification "A file is an entity; its fields follow schema.org's CreativeWork (version, identifier, isPartOf, position) and CodeMeta's software metadata (to verify)" ;
    mz:mappingRelation "subClassOf" ;
    mz:standardTerm "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity" ;
    mz:termIri "https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifr#ReleaseRecord" .

mzid:term-ifr-ReleaseTag a mz:OntologyTerm ;
    rdfs:label "ifr:ReleaseTag"@en ;
    mz:basis mz:Maps ;
    mz:definedBy "0026-works-versioning FR-018" ;
    mz:justification "Git defines the annotated and the signed tag in its manual and publishes no RDF vocabulary, so the mapping names the manual page of git-tag" ;
    mz:mappingRelation "closeMatch" ;
    mz:standardTerm "https://git-scm.com/docs/git-tag" ;
    mz:termIri "https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifr#ReleaseTag" .

mzid:term-ifr-Retention a mz:OntologyTerm ;
    rdfs:label "ifr:Retention"@en ;
    mz:addedOn "2026-11-17" ;
    mz:basis mz:Unaligned ;
    mz:definedBy "0026-works-versioning FR-027" ;
    mz:justification "No standard adopted yet. Examined: ODRL has the action delete and the constraint elapsedTime, which a policy can say as a duty to delete after a period, but it is a policy language and not a record of how long bytes are kept (to verify); ISO 15489 (records management) and PREMIS (preservation metadata) name retention and disposition without a published RDF class for it (to verify); DCAT has no retention term. Decision pending (0018-standards-first FR-005)." ;
    mz:termIri "https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifr#Retention" .

mzid:term-ifr-Tombstone a mz:OntologyTerm ;
    rdfs:label "ifr:Tombstone"@en ;
    mz:addedOn "2026-11-17" ;
    mz:basis mz:Unaligned ;
    mz:definedBy "0026-works-versioning FR-027" ;
    mz:justification "No standard adopted yet. Examined: The DOI and DataCite practice of a tombstone page for a withdrawn record, and HTTP 410 Gone, name the behavior; no standard publishes a class for the record of a version whose bytes are removed but whose digest and metadata remain (to verify DataCite's schema). Decision pending (0018-standards-first FR-005)." ;
    mz:termIri "https://www.intellectualfrontiers.com/ontology/ifr#Tombstone" .

